Two things here are my background knowledge, not something I checked in the papers I read. First, FSDP's `SHARD_GRAD_OP` mode roughly corresponds to ZeRO-2. Second, the FSDP paper's "sharding factor" covers the whole range (p. 4): F = 1 is DDP, F = number of GPUs is full sharding, and values in between give hybrid sharding.

**Tensor parallelism splits a layer’s matrices; context parallelism splits one sequence; expert parallelism splits the experts in an MoE layer.** [1–3]

